1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,480
And lo and behold, it
was the right choice.

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:07,446
Had I not spilled that fateful
cup of coffee, where would I be?

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:08,870
No way!

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,180
It's not possible!

5
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,300
It was supposed to work out!

6
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:14,670
Brat!

7
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:18,520
So you poked your nose around
and found Stray Cat, huh?!

8
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,000
Oh, I bother.

9
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,009
As long as I keep Bites
the Dust activated,

10
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,788
it'll function to keep my secret
and protect you at all cost.

11
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,240
Crap! I blew it!

12
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:39,674
And the others don't have
long before they get blown up!

13
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:42,057
You tried to end me once and for all with

14
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,846
one of Stray Cat's
compressed air projectiles.

15
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,510
Hayato,

16
00:00:46,593 --> 00:00:49,477
there's no way your little pea brain
could have come up with such a clever

17
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:53,897
idea unless you'd already experienced
this morning at least three or four times.

18
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:57,745
The fact that you've lived through
this morning that many times?

19
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:04,860
Is a surefire sign that bites the dust
is destined to eradicate not just Rohan?

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,457
but at least one of
his companions as well.

21
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:10,180
So your loose lips won't only sink Rohan,

22
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:13,615
but whichever one of his
friends you ran your mouth to.

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:17,140
Did the would-be
detectives gang up on you?

24
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:19,322
Who have you murdered this time?

25
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:22,400
Well, was it a runt by the name of Koichi?

26
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:25,037
Or maybe it was Jotaro Kujo.

27
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:28,826
Knowing that he's dead would make
this a red-letter day indeed.

28
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:30,740
It's all over!

29
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:36,089
It'd be far too risky for me to allow
you to relive any more of this morning.

30
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,900
That would expose me to an attack.

31
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,820
So once the others die, I'll
temporarily disengage Bites the Dust.

32
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,337
Bites the Dust is all-powerful!

33
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:55,640
It took a while, but luck is
finally on Yoshikage Kira's side.

34
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,200
Wait a second.

35
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:03,600
That name, Kira, is that your real...

36
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,350
Huh?

37
00:02:05,433 --> 00:02:06,263
Whoopsie.

38
00:02:06,346 --> 00:02:08,662
Did I just reveal my true
name to you by mistake?

39
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:10,650
Indeed.

40
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,919
I'm none other than Yoshikage Kira.

41
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:17,737
You can shout it to the
heavens if it suits your fancy.

42
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:20,080
By the way, do you have the time?

43
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:25,477
You're dead wrong I haven't mentioned
you to anyone I never opened my mouth to!

44
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:31,217
Anyone because I knew exactly what would
happen to them if I did so instead I

45
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:35,177
decided to make a call I remembered he
said he overslept and was running late

46
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:40,557
so I found his number and woke him up
I didn't break any rules I just phoned

47
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:46,237
a friend and remember one thing you're
the one who revealed his own secret?

48
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,150
identity.

49
00:02:47,233 --> 00:02:49,748
I was just stalling for
a bit of extra time.

50
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,979
Time for him to drag himself out of
bed and show up a little earlier.

51
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:28,380
Breakdown! Breakdown!

52
00:03:57,460 --> 00:03:59,080
Night to night,

53
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,697
night is my

54
00:04:01,693 --> 00:04:02,523
Night to night, night is my soul?

55
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:22,215
Breakdown, Breakdown!

56
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,960
Hey, Josuke!

57
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:35,257
Looks like we're gonna make it to
the big meeting on Time After All!

58
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:36,420
Hold it! No.

59
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,420
This guy, he isn't who he says he is.

60
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:42,657
I don't know if it was pure
chance or fate giving us a break?

61
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:44,997
but I heard this guy say a certain name.

62
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,480
I don't believe it.

63
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:51,157
Believe it, asshole, cause I know I just
heard you say the name Yoshikage Kira.

64
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,070
Seriously?

65
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,280
What are the chances?

66
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:56,759
This isn't chance.

67
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,880
It's not fate either.

68
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:02,340
This was making a gamble and
lucky for me it paid off.

69
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,877
Your end has arrived.

70
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,620
Just admit it already.

71
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:08,801
I know I heard the name
slither out of your mouth.

72
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:10,860
It can't be!

73
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,310
Murderer!

74
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:18,517
If it turns out you and him just happened
to share a name, don't you worry.

75
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,040
I can heal if need be.

76
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:22,720
This bastard's really Yoshikage Kira?

77
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,340
Damn that little brat.

78
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,207
I should have known he
would lead me to ruin.

79
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,057
This can't be happening.

80
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:35,880
I have to deactivate Bites the Dust so
I can defend myself from these cretins!

81
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:38,880
Protect me, Deadly Queen!

82
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,630
It's chilly.

83
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,746
Must be due to all this rain.

84
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:59,220
Really, is it too much to ask for
certain people to show up on time?

85
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,820
Oh, there's Koichi and Jotaro.

86
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,740
All right!

87
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,000
I beat the clock!

88
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,460
I defeated destiny!

89
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:23,900
I was never one for rapturous hives. No,

90
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:26,694
so long as I avoided dispiriting loads,

91
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:29,577
I was content to live
as carefree as a daisy.

92
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:33,937
More than anything, I sought to live
a quiet life of peace and tranquility.

93
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,785
You've finally shown yourself!

94
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:37,737
That'll make it real easy to knock that

95
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:40,397
peace and tranquility
right off your new face!

96
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,940
Whoa, it's the dude from Rohan's picture!

97
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:45,897
I would've guessed we'd end
up meeting the guy here!

98
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:49,480
I'm pretty sure we didn't run
into him by chance, Okuyasu.

99
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,437
I haven't figured out all of it,

100
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:54,637
but given that he revealed his
real name to Hayato Kawajiri,

101
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,014
I get the feeling we showed
up just in the nick of time.

102
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:04,377
Before you dullards get
all high and mighty,

103
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:07,989
I should tell you I wasn't
running away despite appearances.

104
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:12,319
I can obliterate any one of you the
instant the thought occurs to me.

105
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,340
I detest conflict.

106
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:19,180
I hate the very idea of it with the
white-hot intensity of a thousand suns.

107
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,857
Conflict runs completely
counter to the peace

108
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,881
and tranquility I strive
for every day of my life.

109
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,697
It's really quite simple to rise
victorious in a single battle.

110
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:32,660
But, of course, the stress begins
to pile up before the next one.

111
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,460
It's a foolish endeavor.

112
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:37,860
To engage in conflict is
to engage in futility.

113
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:42,217
You brought this shit on yourself when
you murdered Shigetsu, you frickin' idiot!

114
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:44,637
You're a sick son of a
bitch who kills for fun!

115
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:49,544
You shouldn't get the privilege of flapping
those stolen gums, you cat-eyed freak!

116
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,277
Watch yourself, Josuke!

117
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:59,440
Make sure you avoid Deadly Queen's
creepy bomb hand at all costs.

118
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:03,777
I've already told you the reason for
my not obliterating all of you earlier.

119
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:06,157
The only souls standing between me and my

120
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,828
eternal peace and
tranquility are you three.

121
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:13,118
Since I've been found out, I have
no choice but to do battle with you.

122
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:16,769
Things are about to get dicey,
Hayato, so get behind us now!

123
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,780
Let's see now.

124
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:21,887
Shining Diamond's range
is one to two meters.

125
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:25,277
And it corrects that which
has been destroyed or altered.

126
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:28,417
I won't be fixin' you up, buddy,
so don't even worry about it!

127
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:31,735
A good ass-kicking's the only
treatment you're getting!

128
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,260
Hey, look out!

129
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,170
Dora.

130
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,440
He's tough.

131
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,017
I can't tell what happened,

132
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:56,377
but Kira hacking up blood and flying
through the air gets a hell yeah from me!

133
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:58,813
Your deadly queen's as slow as molasses.

134
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:01,797
For all the killing you do,
you're a real lethargic fighter.

135
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:04,777
Guess all that peace and
tranquility will do that to ya.

136
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:09,684
It's painfully obvious that your stand
just isn't cut out for one-on-one fighting.

137
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,441
Jousuke, he's slow, but
don't let your guard down!

138
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:17,757
If you wanna knock him around
without laying a finger on him,

139
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:21,311
there's no better stand to have
on your side than the hand!

140
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:22,930
Bring it!

141
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:27,380
You scrape away space
to transport things, eh?

142
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:32,287
Josuke was my target, but it appears fate
has other ideas in mind for me today.

143
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,700
I'm now poised to attack you.

144
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,000
I know, I'll use the Plat!

145
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,490
What?

146
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,200
Nice, direct hit.

147
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,737
That wasn't too bad.

148
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,377
Especially for beginners, luck.

149
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:55,077
What the hell happened?

150
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,517
I didn't see anything. Touch me.

151
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,537
It's the air. The air.

152
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:01,157
Spit some kind of fire.

153
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,180
Okuyasu.

154
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,517
Did I hear him right?

155
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,117
The air spit fire.

156
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,077
But how?

157
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,657
Well, boys.

158
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,637
Do you see?

159
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:15,160
Now this is why I kept my pet.

160
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:19,177
I've found a way to use Stray Cat's air

161
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:22,319
-controlling abilities in
Deadly Queen's explosions.

162
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,937
I must thank you for carting
it all the way here, Hayato.

163
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:29,844
The invisibility of the air mixed
with the power of an explosion.

164
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,837
He couldn't have used a more dangerous
combination of elements if he tried.

165
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:37,117
He was growing it to do this all along.

166
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:40,837
And I'm the wise guy who brought
the stupid thing right to him.

167
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:44,397
I did tell you luck was
finally on my side, didn't I?

168
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:48,245
But the characters that make up
the word luck are bringing life.

169
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,800
How deliciously apropos.

170
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:04,480
Is something wrong, Mr. Jotaro?

171
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,220
No, it's nothing.

172
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:11,875
For a moment I thought I heard Josuke,
but I guess it was just the rain.

173
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:15,277
Quintessential Josuke, I'm
sure the slob overslept again.

174
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:17,357
If he's not here in five minutes flat,

175
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:19,817
I'm going straight to
Hayato Kawajiri's school?

176
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:23,076
and I'll leave you two here
to wait for everyone else.

177
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,580
I'm gonna make you as
good as new, Okuyasu!

178
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:29,761
That's certainly a noble thought.

179
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:34,120
But you see, it's time for you to explode.

180
00:11:34,740 --> 00:11:37,377
That cat plant launched
air at him like a bullet!

181
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:40,000
It can transform air into an explosive!

182
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:42,520
Here it is!

183
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,954
You've got to run now!

184
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,580
You can't see it!

185
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,426
It's that weird bubble thing!

186
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:51,810
Move!

187
00:11:51,893 --> 00:11:53,080
It's gonna get you!

188
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,340
Oh, that's right!

189
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:03,405
He has the power to fix things,
which means he can heal Okuyasu!

190
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:05,360
To fix that which is broken,

191
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:09,856
using your power to reassemble broken
stone into a wall was impressive.

192
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,259
I've got it again!

193
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:15,780
Kay, it's coming!

194
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,797
Nothing in the world is as terrifying?

195
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,380
As the act of assumption!

196
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,997
Especially for those contemptible few!

197
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,597
Who assume the false superiority.

198
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:29,209
of their own talents
and special abilities.

199
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,457
Yo, it's squeezing through!

200
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,599
Contact it and cause it to explode!

201
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:47,489
I thought it would at
least decapitate him.

202
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:51,169
But lucky for him, the destructive
force was rather shallow.

203
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:55,860
My deadly queen's explosion is not
limited to objects it directly touches.

204
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:58,185
Thinking so was an assumption.

205
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,740
It can generate an explosion
at any distance I wish.

206
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,377
No matter where you try
to hide or how quickly

207
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:07,217
you build a protective
stone wall or metal plate,

208
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:10,947
my bomb will slip through any
obstacle and execute its target.

209
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:14,720
You won't escape with your life this time.

210
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,720
Now die.

211
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,580
It's no use.

212
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:23,117
There's no way to dodge it.

213
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,840
What do you mean, dodge it?

214
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:27,260
I have no intention of escaping.

215
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,340
For the record, I would never run away.

216
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:33,080
How else would I heal Okuyasu's wounds?

217
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,320
He's charging right into it.

218
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:41,860
It went around him!

219
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:46,737
I thought you said you could
detonate that thing at any distance.

220
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:48,702
I must have found the exception.

221
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:53,549
Namely, I'm just a little too close for
comfort for you to try blowing me up.

222
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:56,660
Doing that wouldn't end
well for you now, would it?

223
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,640
Alright, hang on.

224
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:03,313
I'll have you healed before you know it.

225
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,496
You can't touch him!

226
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,640
Trust me on this!

227
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,682
If I know Kira, he's
already transformed Okuyasu!

228
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:11,720
He's a bomb!

229
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:17,620
Damn that little whelp. He what? No!

230
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:21,740
I never saw Deadly Queen lay
even a finger on Okuyasu!

231
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,977
What makes you think he
was able to pull that off?

232
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:28,257
You're not a stand user,
so how would you know?

233
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:29,170
I just do!

234
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:32,397
I've lived in the same house as
that psycho until this morning!

235
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,957
His face tells me everything!

236
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,497
His stand touched him
before we could notice!

237
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,417
Josuke, please!

238
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,497
You gotta trust me!

239
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,815
Okuyasu's a bomb now!

240
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,140
Yoshikage Kira!

241
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,350
Easy.

242
00:14:44,433 --> 00:14:47,740
Give me a moment to think.
Well, now. Let's see.

243
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,497
You stormed at me out of the blue,

244
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:51,897
so I can't really say
whether I touched him or not.

245
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:54,497
Actually, the whole
incident was such a blur.

246
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:57,345
Perhaps I should press
the switch and find out.

247
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,917
No! Please don't!

248
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:02,830
I'm begging you!

249
00:15:02,913 --> 00:15:05,417
Just hurry up and shoot
your next air missile!

250
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:07,057
Point the damn thing at me and shoot!

251
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:08,220
Come on! Do it!

252
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:12,857
Really, now, there's no need to be hasty
and end the fun so quickly, is there?

253
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:14,200
Josuke Higashikata,

254
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:16,677
I think I'll observe you
a little while longer

255
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:19,289
and then decide if I
should obliterate you.

256
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:25,029
Besides, you honestly have no real proof
I turned Okuyasu into a bomb at all.

257
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:28,496
It might be possible to heal
him with Shining Diamond.

258
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:30,437
I could be overstepping here,

259
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,417
but at this point it
would appear you have only

260
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:35,337
one course of action if
you want to save Okuyasu.

261
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:38,380
You must heal him by way of touching him.

262
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,940
I don't envy the position you're in.

263
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:44,880
If he is a human bomb,

264
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,277
touching him with Shining
Diamond may kill you,

265
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:51,260
but Okuyasu would be spared the
fate of exploding into oblivion.

266
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:54,960
If you heal your dear
friend's critical injuries,

267
00:15:55,180 --> 00:15:58,004
at least your sacrifice
won't have been in vain.

268
00:15:58,260 --> 00:15:59,090
No!

269
00:15:59,173 --> 00:16:00,003
Don't touch him, Josuke!

270
00:16:00,086 --> 00:16:02,377
I'll wait until you've made your decision.

271
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,940
Do you save your best friend's life?

272
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:08,420
Or do you just attack me and let him die?

273
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,550
Wow.

274
00:16:11,633 --> 00:16:13,977
I'm content to wait until
you make a decision.

275
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:16,857
But it seems you're averse
to touching your friend,

276
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:19,116
even when it means keeping him alive.

277
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:23,618
I have proof touching him is deadly!

278
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:28,578
I know for a fact that Kira's only
able to control one bomb at a time.

279
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:32,297
Once he's activated one
of his freaky bomb things,

280
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:36,517
it's impossible for him to fire off the
next one until the first has been detonated.

281
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,457
Think about it.

282
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:39,117
He only used one at a time.

283
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,917
Why wouldn't he launch a bunch at once?

284
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,017
He's made Okuyasu into a
bomb so he can't shoot now.

285
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,857
Are you trying to make a point?

286
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:50,705
The point is there's still a way to save
Okuyasu, but someone needs to touch him.

287
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,290
Hmm?

288
00:16:54,373 --> 00:16:56,026
Deadly Queen, bomb switch on!

289
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,160
And that someone has gotta be me!

290
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:05,650
Hayato!

291
00:17:07,340 --> 00:17:08,540
Now I get it!

292
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:09,880
Shining Diamond!

293
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:20,260
You're one crazy-ass SOB, Hayato.

294
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:23,499
Took some major balls to
set off the bomb like that.

295
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,817
You sure you're a grade School?

296
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:27,312
Because that was Bites.

297
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,357
Yeah, well, I couldn't
stand around doing nothing,

298
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:32,737
and I knew you had the power to heal me.

299
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:35,467
I refuse to let any more
innocent people die.

300
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:38,397
Besides, if you're gone, he'll
off me in the blink of an eye,

301
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,557
and he'll be free to do whatever he wants.

302
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,097
It's just a matter of time
before he kills my mom,

303
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:45,557
and then he'll go after
more people in this town.

304
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:49,537
But first, you die, though your
power is certainly an issue.

305
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:53,620
To think your stand can reverse my
destructive acts in mere seconds.

306
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,197
I'd almost forgotten
how much that annoying

307
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,780
healing ability of yours vexes me utterly.

308
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:00,420
Deadly Queen!

309
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:03,331
Josuke, he's gonna shoot!

310
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:15,660
It'll detonate on impact so you'll have
no opportunity to guard. Then again,

311
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:18,777
you could sidestep the explosive
if you happen to see it,

312
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:22,357
So I've launched one so small
it's almost impossible to detect.

313
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:26,060
With Okuyasu on your back and
those painful shrapnel wounds,

314
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,320
can you really dodge a projectile?

315
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,417
Just get the hell out of there, Josuke!

316
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,557
If the explosion so much as brushes
against you, you'll be a dead man!

317
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,520
I healed you!

318
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,466
Why haven't you woken up yet?

319
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,900
Open those beady eyes, Okuyasu!

320
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,097
The bomb's on its way!

321
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:41,010
Move it!

322
00:18:41,093 --> 00:18:42,938
Only eight more meters until impact.

323
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,997
All right, enough goofing around, buddy.

324
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,077
It's time to wake up now.

325
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,717
You're as good as new, Okuyasu!

326
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:48,840
Chusuke, please!

327
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:50,177
Seven meters to go.

328
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,637
Don't you leave me, dick!

329
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:53,340
Open your damn eyes! Hey!

330
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:57,720
Come on, man, quit napping and
open your freaking eyes! Hey,

331
00:18:57,960 --> 00:19:02,725
if you wake up, we can knock the shit out
of this asshole just like we always do!

332
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:04,660
Chusuke, go!

333
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:08,746
Like joe montana throwing the
touchdown pass of a winning game,

334
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:11,377
i'll detonate the sucker
in the perfect position.

335
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,820
and go home victorious.

336
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,280
Four meters until impact.

337
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,460
Go! Right now!

338
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,417
You've gotta run for it or
it's gonna hit you dead on!

339
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:23,137
I'm so sorry about Okuyasu,
but he's already...

340
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:24,280
No, don't say it!

341
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,897
The only one of us who needs
to run here is you, kid!

342
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,600
Two meters till showtime.

343
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:32,585
With a three meter radius, they're
sure to die in the explosion.

344
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,600
I can see it!

345
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:39,073
It's two meters in front of
you and it's closing in fast!

346
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,475
You've gotta run now!

347
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:41,677
Listen to me, Josuke!

348
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:43,300
Okuyasu's gone! He's dead!

349
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,337
Accept it already!

350
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:46,420
He's nowhere near dead, dammit!

351
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:49,857
He's back in top form and he'll
open his eyes any minute now!

352
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:54,480
Yes, just one more meter and then
pop goes the riff-raff. Josuke!

353
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:03,740
Holy heck!

354
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:06,158
It was ruptured by a blade of blood!

355
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:08,977
Did Josuke somehow take
his blood and propel

356
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:11,117
it with so much force
that it cut like a knife?

357
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,380
Oh, yeah.

358
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,557
It's just like that time in the attic.

359
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:18,758
The air shackles deflated when I
punctured them with a compass needle.

360
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:25,880
He used the blood from his wound
like a water jet cutter. Hmph.

361
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:28,337
And he severed the bullet clean through.

362
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:31,080
Nice try, but it didn't do you any good.

363
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,040
You gotta move!

364
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,157
They didn't deflate!

365
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:39,181
This improvised air bullet explosive
is stabilized by Deadly Queen,

366
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,060
so it won't deflate.

367
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:44,037
You can split it, smash
it, or dice it to pieces.

368
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:47,532
But I'm pleased to say the
bomb will never lose its power.

369
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:50,860
And now, back to our
regularly scheduled explosion.

370
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,270
Touchdown.

371
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:55,880
What the heck's going on?

372
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,860
He's floating?

373
00:20:58,760 --> 00:20:59,590
Explode.

374
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,420
No, this isn't floating!

375
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:12,997
Shining Diamond won't
allow me to heal myself,

376
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,457
which, to be frank, would
come in handy right now.

377
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,557
But when it comes to pieces of road,

378
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,993
like the ones that got lodged
in me from the first blast,

379
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,604
that's a whole different story.

380
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:27,360
What a super neat idea, using
the road to pull you up.

381
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,257
I'm out of options.

382
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:33,987
You don't live here, but it'll
work as our safe house for now.

383
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,720
Please, you have to leave Okuyasu.

384
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,897
If you keep carrying him
around, you're gonna get killed.

385
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:42,157
He'll find a way to corner
you, and that'll be it!

386
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:44,740
I asked you to keep quiet, so drop it!

387
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:47,337
Okuyasu and I have a connection.

388
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,257
He's my friend.

389
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:49,417
I won't abandon him.

390
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:51,457
No, that's not what I'm trying to say!

391
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:54,599
By the time you healed
Okuyasu, he was already dead!

392
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:56,370
Enough!

393
00:21:56,453 --> 00:21:57,283
Enough.

394
00:21:57,366 --> 00:21:58,196
Not another word. I mean it.

395
00:21:58,279 --> 00:22:00,944
You've got to focus your
energy on beating Kira!

396
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,640
How irksome.

397
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:08,000
That blasted ability to correct.

398
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,712
Without it, my bomb would be unstoppable.

399
00:22:11,020 --> 00:22:13,857
I see now that the greatest
obstacle standing in the

400
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:17,175
way of my attaining peace
and tranquility isn't Jotaro.

401
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,260
It's him.

402
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:24,900
Josuke Higashikata.

403
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:34,520
I want you, but I don't know if I
need you, but I'm trying to find you.
